    readTime: 7,
    intro: 'An estimate is a prediction, and the only way to know whether your predictions are profitable is to track what each job actually costs against what you quoted. Too many fence contractors win jobs and complete them without ever knowing which ones made money and which lost it, because they never compare actual costs to the estimate. This blind spot means repeating profitable jobs and unprofitable ones alike, with no way to tell the difference. The contractors who steadily improve their margins are the ones who measure every job against its estimate and learn from the gaps. This article covers how to track real costs during the install, how to compare them to the estimate meaningfully, and how a connected platform captures the cost data automatically so the comparison becomes a routine insight rather than a forensic project.',
